      "explanation": "The erector spinae muscle is part of the deep back muscles and receives its motor innervation from the dorsal rami of spinal nerves. These branches provide segmental motor innervation to the deep back muscles and also provide sensory innervation to the skin of the back. The ventral rami of spinal nerves contribute to the innervation of the anterolateral trunk and limbs. The thoracodorsal nerve innervates the latissimus dorsi muscle, the accessory nerve innervates the trapezius muscle and sternocleidomastoid muscle, and the dorsal scapular nerve primarily innervates the rhomboid major muscle, rhomboid minor muscle, and levator scapulae muscle."
