      "explanation": "The pyramidalis muscle is a small triangular muscle located anterior to the inferior part of the rectus abdominis muscle. It originates from the pubic symphysis and pubic crest, and its muscle fibers run superiorly to insert into the linea alba. Its primary function is to tense the linea alba. The pyramidalis muscle may be completely absent in some individuals."
