    explanation: "Barrett esophagus represents metaplastic replacement of the normal stratified squamous epithelium of the esophagus by intestinal-type columnar epithelium, which may contain goblet cells. This condition most commonly develops in association with chronic gastroesophageal reflux and is associated with an increased risk of esophageal adenocarcinoma."
