    explanation: "Lymph from the terminal ileum primarily drains into the ileocolic lymph nodes, which are located around the junction of the ileum and ascending colon and belong to the regional lymph nodes along branches of the superior mesenteric artery. Lymphatic drainage from the small intestine generally passes through mesenteric lymph nodes toward the intestinal lymphatic trunk and subsequently to the cisterna chyli."
