      "explanation": "The membranous part of the trachea forms its posterior wall and consists of connective tissue and the trachealis muscle. Excessively deep insertion of an instrument or tracheostomy tube can injure this structure, potentially causing bleeding and air leakage into the surrounding tissues. The tracheal cartilages form the anterior and lateral portions of the tracheal wall. The cricotracheal ligament lies between the cricoid cartilage and the first tracheal ring. The median cricothyroid ligament and thyrohyoid membrane are fibrous structures of the larynx located more superiorly."
