      "correct": "a",
      "explanation": "The loop of Henle consists of descending and ascending limbs and extends from the renal cortex into the medulla. The thin descending limb is highly permeable to water, whereas the ascending limb is impermeable to water and allows ion transport. This differential permeability is essential for establishing the osmotic gradient in the renal medulla, which enables urine concentration. The proximal convoluted tubule precedes the loop of Henle, whereas the distal convoluted tubule continues from its ascending limb. Collecting ducts are not part of the nephron, and the glomerulus is part of the renal corpuscle."
