      "explanation": "The tuber cinereum is part of the hypothalamus and forms part of the floor of the third ventricle. It is located between the optic chiasm anteriorly and the mammillary bodies posteriorly, and its central part extends into the infundibulum, which connects the hypothalamus with the pituitary gland. The habenular trigone and pineal gland belong to the dorsal part of the diencephalon, the lateral geniculate body lies on the lateral aspect of the midbrain, and the lamina terminalis forms the anterior wall of the third ventricle."
