    correct: "a",
    explanation: "The patient in image A has acromegaly, which results from excessive production of growth hormone (GH), most commonly due to a somatotroph adenoma of the anterior pituitary. Typical features of acromegaly include enlargement and thickening of the nose, prominent cheekbones, prominent supraorbital ridges, frontal bossing, thickened lips, coarsening of facial features, and a prominent mandible (prognathism). Excessive GH production leads, via IGF-1, to increased growth of bones and soft tissues, explaining these characteristic facial changes.\nIn image B, number 1 indicates the anterior pituitary (adenohypophysis), which contains somatotroph cells that produce GH. Number 2 indicates the posterior pituitary (neurohypophysis), which does not produce GH. Number 3 indicates the thalamus. Number 4 indicates the corpus callosum, and number 5 indicates the sphenoid sinus."
