    correct: "a",
    explanation: "The dens artery sign is an early sign of acute occlusion of a cerebral artery by a thrombus, which causes increased attenuation of the affected artery on non-contrast CT. The middle cerebral artery primarily supplies the lateral portions of the frontal, parietal, and temporal lobes. In contrast, the anterior cerebral artery primarily supplies the medial portions of the frontal and parietal lobes, whereas the posterior cerebral artery primarily supplies the occipital lobe and inferomedial portion of the temporal lobe."
