      "explanation": "The hypoglossal nerve (CN XII) provides motor innervation to all intrinsic muscles of the tongue and three extrinsic muscles of the tongue: the genioglossus muscle, hyoglossus muscle, and styloglossus muscle. The palatoglossus muscle is the exception among the extrinsic muscles of the tongue and is innervated by the vagus nerve."
