      "explanation": "The round ligament of the uterus passes through the inguinal canal and continues through the superficial inguinal ring toward the labium majus. It develops from the inferior aspect of the ovarian gubernaculum and helps maintain the anteverted position of the uterus. In males, the spermatic cord passes through the inguinal canal and contains structures associated with the testis and ductus deferens."
