      "explanation": "The cell bodies of the primary sensory neurons of the auditory pathway are located in the spiral ganglion, which lies within the modiolus of the cochlea. These neurons are bipolar, with peripheral processes extending to the receptor cells of the organum spirale, while their central processes form the cochlear part of the vestibulocochlear nerve and terminate in the cochlear nuclei. The vestibular ganglion contains the cell bodies of neurons of the vestibular part of the vestibulocochlear nerve. The cochlear nuclei and the lateral vestibular nucleus are central nervous system nuclei, not ganglia containing the cell bodies of primary sensory neurons."
