      "correct": "a",
      "explanation": "The subthalamic nucleus lies in the subthalamic region, ventral to the thalamus and medial to the internal capsule. The internal capsule separates laterally located basal ganglia structures, particularly the lentiform nucleus, from structures located medially. The external capsule lies lateral to the putamen, whereas the extreme capsule is located lateral to the claustrum. The corpus callosum and superior longitudinal fasciculus do not have this topographic relationship to the subthalamic nucleus."
