      "correct": "a",
      "explanation": "The glossopharyngeal nerve (IX) carries preganglionic parasympathetic fibers from the inferior salivatory nucleus. These fibers travel through the tympanic nerve and then the tympanic plexus, from which the lesser petrosal nerve continues to the otic ganglion. After synapsing in the otic ganglion, postganglionic fibers travel through the auriculotemporal nerve to the parotid gland, where they stimulate salivary secretion. The facial nerve (VII) provides parasympathetic innervation to the lacrimal gland and some salivary glands but not to the parotid gland. The vagus nerve (X) does not provide the main parasympathetic secretomotor innervation to the parotid gland. The mandibular nerve (V3) gives rise to the auriculotemporal nerve, which carries the postganglionic parasympathetic fibers, but the preganglionic parasympathetic fibers originate from the glossopharyngeal nerve (IX). The hypoglossal nerve (XII) is a motor nerve supplying the muscles of the tongue."
